# Test: a plugin that declares restart and exits is started again
#
# The plugin is a REAL external process the daemon forks from its `run` line.
# Its first generation completes the five-stage handshake and then returns,
# which ends the process. Nothing else happens: no operator acts, no config is
# reloaded, no signal is sent. The daemon has to notice the exit on its own,
# read what the plugin declared, and start it again.
#
# The second generation is what proves it, because it can only exist if the
# daemon started one. It says so and then asks the daemon to stop, which is what
# ends this test.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-1 -- a plugin that declares failure-policy restart and exits is
# running again, through the real fork-and-handshake path.
# PREVENTS: the state this spec found. ProcessManager.Respawn had one caller, a
# config-reload rollback, so nothing in the daemon watched a plugin process exit
# and a crashed plugin stayed dead for the life of the daemon.

tmpfs=ze-bgp.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external failure-restart {
		run "ze-test fixture plugin/failure-policy-restart"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze start ze-bgp.conf:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=FIXTURE: failure-restart generation 1 is exiting
expect=stderr:contains=plugin exited, starting it again
expect=stderr:contains=OK: the plugin process was started again after it exited
